item RefillStock qty;pos;shp
⍝ Increases the quantity of a selected product to refill inventory stock.
⍝ As a left argument write 'name'. As a right argument write quantity.
pos ← ItemName⍳⊂item
shp ← ⍴ItemName

:If shp<pos
⎕←'Item Not Found'

:ElseIf qty>50
⎕←'Exceded maximum of products! Refill with less stocks'

:ElseIf (Quantity[pos]+qty)>100
 ⎕←'Too much products! Try with less.'
:Else
Quantity[pos] ← Quantity[pos] + qty
Costs ← Costs + ((Price[pos] × 0.25) × qty)

⎕← 'Item name: ' , item
⎕← ' is refilled with: ' , qty , ' of stocks.'
⎕←''
⎕←' Quantity of the item after refill: ' , Quantity[pos]
⎕←''
⎕←'Costs of purchase: ' ,  ((Price[pos] × 0.25) × qty)
⎕←''
⎕←'Total costs: ' , Costs
:EndIf
